  "id": "COMPOUND:1727 - PROTEIN:5848",
  "verbalization": "Castanospermine is shown to interact with the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, and Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate. All these compounds are linked to the Raji cell line, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving this enzyme. The shared target indicates that Castanospermine may exert its effects through a common pathway, possibly by inhibiting the enzyme and thereby affecting sialylation processes in Raji cells. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same enzyme supports the hypothesis that Castanospermine could act through this pathway, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Castanospermine and Raji cells, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific role of the enzyme in this relationship.",
